note: a triage ranking was applied to the wrong axis — the corpus's top
  codes by raw rows included pin-authoring probes (agents *writing* refusal
  tests) counted as organic pain, and a high-firing umbrella contract code
  (KORU161) ranked as "message fails to teach" while most of its sites
  already taught. Declares that intent and kind must split a family before
  the fix-vs-teach ranking runs. First measured instance: KORU161, ~30 of
  ~128 systemic rows kind:pin; teach-miss, not count, decided DIAG vs DOC.
